 "preregistered": {
  "estimators": "Per state and patch: the raw score mean with an empirical-Bernstein 95% interval (Maurer-Pontil Theorem 4, range 1, unbiased sample variance, two-sided) and the kernel-outcome fraction (z2 = -1 and t = +1) with a Wilson 95% interval. The readout-corrected score applies the inverse tensor product of the four single-qubit assignment matrices of the witness batch's nearest readout-0 and readout-1 (the earlier batch on a tie, the pairing in readout_pairing) and carries a 95% percentile interval of a seeded parametric bootstrap of 4000 draws that redraws the witness outcome counts (multinomial) and every assignment rate from the reference counts (binomial), reported beside the raw interval.",
  "contraction": "A depolarizing contraction V of the (q3, q1, q0) parity gives kernel and bright states (1 - V)/2 and (1 + V)/2, so kernel + bright - 1 is consistent with zero for each partner pair (k_i, b_i) of a batch and pooled over the four pairs of a patch, and middle and sector states read 1/2. A violation at |z| >= 3 names a multi-qubit error outside the contraction, such as an entangling coherent error or leakage. The law is blind to a phase between the two GHZ branches (kernel and bright scores move by (1 -+ cos phi) V/2 and still sum to one), to single-qubit coherent errors and to readout bias; the quadrature batch reads the branch phase, and readout bias is read from the corrected score. Each z divides the raw residual by the square root of the summed sample variances over shots.",
  "quadrature": "Circuits that read q3 in the X basis give <X3 X1 Y0> = -s sin(phi) V for a GHZ pair (|a> + s e^{i phi}|~a>)/sqrt2 with a3 = 0, a0 = 1, while the Y-basis parity of the witnesses gives <Y3 X1 Y0> = s cos(phi) V. With S = (m_b1 - m_k1)/2 from the quadrature circuits and C = (m_k1 - m_b1)/2 from the witnesses of the same patch, phi = atan2(S, C), V = hypot(S, C); (m_k1 + m_b1)/2 of both bases and the e7 parity are null statistics.",
  "pooling": "Patches are analyzed separately; the pooled value is the equal-weight mean over the three patches of the per-patch pooled kernel + bright - 1.",
  "stop_conditions": "Batch 0's readout-0 or readout-1 shows a patch qubit with P(1|0) or P(0|1) above 0.15: stop and redraw the placement. Two successive readout-0 circuits move a patch qubit's P(1|0), or two successive readout-1 circuits move its P(0|1), by more than 0.02: stop. A job fails or returns fewer shots than requested. The account-wide pause or the three-circuit limit would be broken."
 },
